# the argument of aquinas-economy-objection.md by rule (phil/skeleton): connectives from the parse, an atom to each clause
atom	c2_further_superfluou	2 Further it is superfluous to suppose that what can be accounted for by a few principles has been produced by many
atom	seem_everyth_see	but it seems that everything we see in the world can be accounted for by other principles supposing God did not exist
atom	natural_thing_reduc	for all natural things can be reduced to one principle which is nature
atom	reduc_principle_human(x)	x: can be reduced to one principle which is human reason or will
atom	voluntary_thing(x)	x: voluntary things
atom	need_suppose_god(x)	x: need to suppose God's existence
P1	S1	true
P2	S2	c2_further_superfluou
P3	S3	seem_everyth_see
P4	S4	natural_thing_reduc
P5	S4	(all x: voluntary_thing(x) -> reduc_principle_human(x))
C	S5	(all x: need_suppose_god(x) -> !true(x))
